files: pie.glb (model/gltf-binary), pie.generated_image_url.jpeg (image/jpeg)
each file lands in your folder under its name, and its `fetched:` line names its /cdn/ address, the one the world uses. With no `fetched:` line below, `spawn tripo status 6dda13fc-20dc-4cec-8d64-d6d26fd404bd --out pie.glb` lands them.
facing: a workshop file, so it faces the way its bytes do: Tripo puts the side that pie.generated_image_url.jpeg shows on +X. Set model.forward to where the subject faces there: toward you "+x", away "-x", to the picture's left "+z", to its right no forward.
next: `spawn tripo texture 6dda13fc-20dc-4cec-8d64-d6d26fd404bd`, `spawn tripo segment 6dda13fc-20dc-4cec-8d64-d6d26fd404bd`, `spawn tripo rig 6dda13fc-20dc-4cec-8d64-d6d26fd404bd`, `spawn tripo retopo 6dda13fc-20dc-4cec-8d64-d6d26fd404bd --face_limit <n>` or `spawn tripo convert 6dda13fc-20dc-4cec-8d64-d6d26fd404bd --format FBX` take this task by its id; finish by hand in Blender.
